# Offline oracle note — bands-spin-si (PW collinear spin bands, diamond Si)

## Purpose

Character / wall twin for `regressions/pw/bands-spin-si`. **Not** an absolute
eigenvalue pin: CP2K Quickstep uses GTH-PADE + DZVP-GTH; Atomiverse PW uses
ONCV UPF. Record CP2K version, wall, and indirect-gap character when a binary
is available.

## Suggested CP2K settings (mirror closed-shell `si_bands_dos_note.inp` + LSD)

```
&GLOBAL
  PROJECT si_bands_spin_wall
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
  PRINT_LEVEL MEDIUM
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    LSD                          ! collinear spin
    MULTIPLICITY 1               ! M = 0 closed-shell collinear
    &QS
      EPS_DEFAULT 1.0E-10
    &END QS
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 300
      REL_CUTOFF 60
    &END MGRID
    &SCF
      SCF_GUESS ATOMIC
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-6
      MAX_SCF 50
      &DIAGONALIZATION
        ALGORITHM STANDARD
      &END DIAGONALIZATION
      &MIXING
        METHOD BROYDEN_MIXING
        ALPHA 0.4
      &END MIXING
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PADE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &KPOINTS
      SCHEME MONKHORST-PACK 2 2 2
    &END KPOINTS
    &PRINT
      &BAND_STRUCTURE
        ADDED_MOS 4
        &KPOINT_SET
          NPOINTS 4
          SPECIAL_POINT GAMMA 0.0 0.0 0.0
          SPECIAL_POINT X 0.5 0.0 0.5
          SPECIAL_POINT W 0.5 0.25 0.75
          SPECIAL_POINT L 0.5 0.5 0.5
          SPECIAL_POINT GAMMA 0.0 0.0 0.0
          SPECIAL_POINT K 0.375 0.375 0.75
        &END KPOINT_SET
      &END BAND_STRUCTURE
    &END PRINT
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      A 0.0 2.715 2.715
      B 2.715 0.0 2.715
      C 2.715 2.715 0.0
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      Si 0.0 0.0 0.0
      Si 1.3575 1.3575 1.3575
    &END COORD
    &KIND Si
      BASIS_SET DZVP-GTH-q4
      POTENTIAL GTH-PADE-q4
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
```

## Pins written to REFERENCE.md

See `regressions/pw/bands-spin-si/REFERENCE.md`. Literature: Yin–Cohen LDA
Γ→X ~0.45 eV; α≈β and \(M=0\) from fixed occupations.
